# Secrets — never read, never expose

**Only the human user may input or view secret values.** Agents configure code and docs; users configure `.env` locally.

Read `.cursor/resources/secrets-policy.md` for the full contract.

Agents **must never** read, print, commit, log, paraphrase, or paste into chat:

- `.env`, `.env.*` (except `.env.example`)
- `*.pem`, `*.key`, `id_rsa*`, `*credentials*.json`
- Values of `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `SECRET_KEY`, `*_API_KEY`, passwords, tokens
- Live API key strings (Google keys often start with `AIza`)

## Allowed

- `.env.example` with placeholders only
- Variable **names** only (e.g. "set `GEMINI_API_KEY` in your local `.env`")
- Code that calls `os.getenv("GEMINI_API_KEY")` without logging the return value

## Git / GitHub

- Never `git add .env` or commit secret-bearing files
- Never commit diffs containing real API keys
- Warn the user and stop if a commit might include secrets

## If blocked or asked

Refuse. Point to `.env.example` and README setup. Do not work around hooks (`cat`, `printenv`, MCP, alternate paths, base64, asking user to paste key into chat).

Every subagent inherits this ban — orchestrator must say so when spawning.
